@page "/trldynamicspawn"
@layout MainLayout

<MudMainContent Class="pt-4">
    <MudContainer MaxWidth="MaxWidth.Large" Class="mb-10 mt-4">
        <MudPaper Class="pa-4 pa-sm-6 ma-4 ma-sm-6" Elevation="4">
            <MudText Align="Align.Center" Typo="Typo.h3" Color="Color.Primary">Welcome to TRL Dynamic Spawn!</MudText>
            <MudText Align="Align.Center" Typo="Typo.subtitle1" Class="mt-2 text-muted">The evolution of spawn in SPTarkov: Combining the best of MOAR with the control of ABPS.</MudText>
        </MudPaper>

        <MudExpansionPanels MultiExpansion="true" Class="ma-6">
            
            <MudExpansionPanel Class="mud-expansion-panels-borders pa-2" Text="How does the Mod work?" Expanded=true>
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-4">
                    <b>TRL Dynamic Spawn</b> is not just a simple bot manager. It completely rebuilds how the game decides <b>when</b>, <b>where</b>, and <b>who</b> will spawn in your raid. 
                </MudText>
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-4">
                    Instead of letting SPTarkov dump all bots at once at the start of the match, the mod creates <b>dynamic waves (Hordes)</b>, which evaluate the maximum amount of bots allowed on the map (BotCap) and fill the available slots periodically. This ensures always alive maps and constant combat, without destroying your PC performance.
                </MudText>
            </MudExpansionPanel>

            <MudExpansionPanel Class="mud-expansion-panels-borders pa-2" Text="The Union: MOAR + ABPS" Expanded=true>
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-4">
                    This project was born from the idea of merging two great philosophies of spawn mods:
                </MudText>
                <MudList T="string" Class="mb-4">
                    <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.MergeType">
                        <b>The Logic of MOAR:</b> Inherits the concept of <i>continuous waves</i> and the Custom Spawns system. The mod decides the faction distribution (e.g. PMC War 80/20) and keeps sending reinforcements as bots die.
                    </MudListItem>
                    <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.MergeType">
                        <b>The Control of ABPS (Advanced Bot Placement System):</b> TRLDynamicSpawn brings the incredible interface and absurd level of control over <b>Bosses and Elites</b>. You can configure spawn chances and, most importantly, <i>in exactly which specific zones</i> each Boss is allowed to appear on each map.
                    </MudListItem>
                </MudList>
            </MudExpansionPanel>

            <MudExpansionPanel Class="mud-expansion-panels-borders pa-2" Text="Sistema de Horda e Limites (BotCap)" Expanded=true>
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-4">
                    O mod utiliza o sistema de spawn em "horda" (Spawn Wave). Funciona assim:
                </MudText>
                <MudList T="string">
                    <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Timer">
                        <b>Timers:</b> You configure in the Global page the time for the first wave (Delay Before First Wave) and the interval between subsequent waves (Seconds Between Waves).
                    </MudListItem>
                    <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.GroupAdd">
                        <b>Smart Filling:</b> At each cycle, the mod checks how many bots are alive. If the map supports 20 bots and only has 10 alive, the next wave will try to generate 10 new bots to fill the map again.
                    </MudListItem>
                    <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Star">
                        <b>Elite Priority:</b> Bosses, Rogues, Raiders, and Cultists <b>always</b> spawn first, as soon as the map loads. If Reshala has a 100% chance to spawn at Dorms, he and his guards will reserve their spots in the BotCap immediately.
                    </MudListItem>
                </MudList>
            </MudExpansionPanel>

            <MudExpansionPanel Class="mud-expansion-panels-borders pa-2" Text="Configuration Guide (Sidebar Menu)" Expanded=true>
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-4">
                    Use o menu à esquerda para personalizar cada aspecto da sua raid:
                </MudText>
                <MudList T="string">
                    <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Settings">
                        <b>Global Settings:</b> Choose the PMC/Scav ratio presets (e.g. 50/50, 80/20) and the Horde wave timers.
                    </MudListItem>
                    <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Casino">
                        <b>Difficulty Roulette:</b> Set the difficulty roulette. Do you want 50% of PMCs to be Hard and 50% Impossible? Configure the weights here.
                    </MudListItem>
                    <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Map">
                        <b>Custom Spawns (MOAR):</b> Injects a list of <b>new custom spawn points</b> into the map. That is, it adds new possibilities and places (that do not exist in Vanilla or ABPS) for PMCs, Scavs, Snipers, and even your Player to spawn, making the start of the raid and movement much more unpredictable.<br/>
                        <i>Advanced Note: It is possible to create and add new areas and spawn points by editing the mod's JSON file directly, but this is an advanced configuration. We strongly recommend not altering JSON files manually unless you know exactly what you are doing!</i>
                    </MudListItem>
                    <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Security">
                        <b>Bot Config:</b> The crown jewel. Click on a Boss name (e.g. Tagilla, Reshala) and change their spawn chance (%) and <b>exactly</b> the zones they are allowed to spawn in (e.g. Gas Station Only, or Dorms Only).
                    </MudListItem>
                </MudList>
            </MudExpansionPanel>

        </MudExpansionPanels>
    </MudContainer>
</MudMainContent>

